      "source": [
        "# Module 04: Linear Regression"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "dd32629e",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# packages\n",
        "import numpy as np \n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from matplotlib.pyplot import subplots\n",
        "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split \n",
        "from ISLP import load_data\n",
        "from ISLP.models import (ModelSpec as MS, summarize)\n",
        "\n",
        "# set seed\n",
        "seed = 4721"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "1bbffdac",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### We'll use the _Bikeshare_ data from ISLP for this activity. The metadata for _Bikeshare_ can be found [here](https://intro-stat-learning.github.io/ISLP/datasets/Bikeshare.html)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "1cd8a441",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Load the data\n",
        "Bike = load_data('Bikeshare')\n",
        "Bike.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8f05cc6d",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Determine the number of rows and columns in the dataset by returning its \"shape\" attribute."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "7f84fca9",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "Bike.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "a2e246b7",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Determine whether each feature is numeric or categorical by returning the \"dtype\" attribute for each column"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "8c6a3b93",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "Bike.dtypes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "6ac3df98",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Before doing any other analyses, let's create training and test sets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "7c559e11",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "Train, Test = train_test_split(Bike, \n",
        "                               random_state=seed, \n",
        "                               test_size=0.40, \n",
        "                               shuffle=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "b315e2b0",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### We'll treat `bikers` as our response variable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "4cda59b9",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "Train.columns"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "7f6a7f20",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Create a simple regression model predicting bikers from temperature.\n",
        "\n",
        "Because bikers is skewed, we will use log(bikers) as the response."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "74b2a9bb",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X = Train[['temperature']]\n",
        "y = np.log(Train['bikers'])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "2f3fc1ef",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Fit the regression model using statsmodels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "f23d4bc8",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X_sm = sm.add_constant(X)\n",
        "model = sm.OLS(y, X_sm).fit()\n",
        "model.summary()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d2206f15",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Plot log(bikers) vs temperature, along with the regression line."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "6e2a19ce",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
        "plt.scatter(Train['temperature'], np.log(Train['bikers']), alpha=0.5)\n",
        "x_line = np.linspace(Train['temperature'].min(), Train['temperature'].max(), 100)\n",
        "y_line = model.params['const'] + model.params['temperature'] * x_line\n",
        "plt.plot(x_line, y_line)\n",
        "plt.xlabel('temperature')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('log(bikers)')\n",
        "plt.title('log(bikers) vs temperature with regression line')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "30b4ec9c",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Use ModelSpec() to fit the same model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "8c10a648",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "spec = MS(['temperature'])\n",
        "X_design = spec.fit_transform(Train)\n",
        "y_log = np.log(Train['bikers'])\n",
        "model2 = sm.OLS(y_log, X_design).fit()\n",
        "model2.summary()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "c9b1c1a5",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Compare predictions on the test set using RMSE (on the log scale)."
      ]
    },
